## Basic 3D transformations
Here is an example of dynamic rotation matrix applied on 3D primitive and updated by an external slider:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Basic 3D transformations
Here is an example of dynamic rotation matrix applied on 3D primitive and updated by an external slider:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
rot = RotationMatrix[45 Degree, {0, 0, 1.0}];
stair = GeometricTransformation[Cuboid[{0, 0, 0}, {1.5, 1.5, .2}], 
  Table[{RotationMatrix[a, {0, 0, 1}], {Cos[a], Sin[a], a}}, {a, 0, 
    4 Pi, .2}]];

    
Graphics3D[GeometricTransformation[stair, rot // Offload]]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Manipulator

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Manipulator

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
EventHandler[InputRange[0, 180.0 Degree, 1.0 Degree], 
  Function[angle, rot = RotationMatrix[angle, {0, 0, 1.0}]]]

